Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Guernsey_Literary_and_Potato_Peel_Pie_Society_(film)"},{"title":"Laser skin resurfacing","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laser_skin_resurfacing"},{"title":"Chemical peel","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chemical_peel"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Skin","chain":["Carbon lotion applied and laser pulses delivered","Surface skin and oil are exfoliated","Smoother texture and brighter-looking skin"],"effect":"claimed","text":"Clinics offer it for fresher, smoother-looking skin and tighter-looking pores with minimal downtime. People book it before events for an immediate glow."},"wikipedia":{"title":"The Guernsey Literary and Potato Peel Pie Society (film)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Guernsey_Literary_and_Potato_Peel_Pie_Society_(film)"},"grokipedia":null,"lead":["The carbon laser peel, often marketed as the Hollywood peel, is a clinic laser treatment aimed at smoother skin texture, smaller-looking pores and a brighter complexion with little downtime. A carbon-based lotion is applied to the face and then treated with laser pulses; the lotion is said to absorb the energy and lift debris and surface skin.","Laser resurfacing as a category is described in medical references as controlled wounding that prompts skin to regenerate, using ablative, non-ablative and fractional lasers.[1] Peel-style treatments of the surface skin more broadly are covered under chemical peels.[2] The specific carbon-lotion procedure has no published trials in the sources reviewed."],"infobox":[["Type","Laser skin treatment"],["Also called","Hollywood peel, carbon peel"],["Applied by","Clinic practitioner"],["Used for","Pores, texture, dullness"]],"sections":[{"h":"Description","paras":["Practitioners describe the treatment as a carbon lotion plus laser session, with a brief appointment and quick return to normal activity. Laser resurfacing in general ranges from ablative lasers like CO2 and Er:YAG to non-ablative and fractional devices.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found. Related research on laser resurfacing and chemical peels is described generally in medical references.[1][2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Reported risks","paras":["Laser resurfacing in general carries risks of scarring, hyperpigmentation, acne flares and herpes outbreaks.[1] Chemical peels can cause redness, pigment changes and photosensitivity, rising with depth.[2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"In looksmaxxing culture","paras":["It is discussed alongside other skin-texture treatments, with popular interest tied to celebrity-style red-carpet skin."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[],"refs":[{"title":"Laser skin resurfacing","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laser_skin_resurfacing","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Chemical peel","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chemical_peel","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[{"title":"Laser skin resurfacing","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laser_skin_resurfacing","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"kind":null},{"title":"Chemical peel","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chemical_peel","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"kind":null}],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Atlas13 Burning the Boats","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/atlas13-burning-the-boats/259312","site":"T Nation · 3714 posts · 2019"},{"title":"The physiques that made you want to lift?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/the-physiques-that-made-you-want-to-lift/294681","site":"T Nation · 113 posts · 2026"},{"title":"How Hollywood Thinks We Live","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/how-hollywood-thinks-we-live/122971","site":"T Nation · 112 posts · 2009"},{"title":"To The Citizens of America","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/to-the-citizens-of-america/118537","site":"T Nation · 76 posts · 2008"},{"title":"Canadian Al Qaeda","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/canadian-al-qaeda/65846","site":"T Nation · 38 posts · 2006"},{"title":"Dear America, Happy Goodbye Independe